          "filename": "Quarry tramroad, Isle of Portland - geograph.org.uk - 942686.jpg",
          "caption": "Quarry tramroad, Isle of Portland. A considerable network of tramways grew up in and around the many stone quarries on Portland.  Here two rows of stone sleeper blocks in Tout Quarry mark the course of such a line, pointing towards the bricked-up portal of one of at least three tunnels at different levels passing under Wide Street into quarries to the east of the road.",
